{
  "format": "WFScriptPanel",
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Self-contained 10-Page RC low/high-pass laboratory: theory, simulation, AD3 capture, Notebook, full least-squares derivation, annotated source guide and synthetic/real fit-residual explorer.",
  "scriptName": "ACNetworkLaboratory.js",
  "activePageId": "mission",
  "lifecycle": {
    "initializeEnabled": true,
    "shutdownEnabled": true
  },
  "appearance": {
    "themeMode": "dark",
    "background": "",
    "showDesignGrid": false
  },
  "pages": [
    {
      "id": "mission",
      "name": "00  START / MISSION",
      "width": 1460,
      "height": 985,
      "controls": [
        {
          "id": "hero",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "AC NETWORK LAB    /    FROM THEORY TO REAL DATA",
          "x": 22,
          "y": 14,
          "width": 1416,
          "height": 58,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Plain Text",
            "wordWrap": false,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heroSub",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "Portable RC laboratory: predict → simulate → wire → measure → analyze → explain the algorithm. Pages 07–09 show least squares from equations to measured residuals.",
          "x": 22,
          "y": 78,
          "width": 1416,
          "height": 64,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Plain Text",
            "wordWrap": true,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "journeyTitle",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "YOUR LAB JOURNEY  /  45–75 MINUTES",
          "x": 22,
          "y": 152,
          "width": 1416,
          "height": 40,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Plain Text",
            "wordWrap": false,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "mission1",
          "type": "instruction_card",
          "text": "01  MODEL THE CIRCUIT",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 208,
          "width": 454,
          "height": 148,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "Choose Low-pass or High-pass. Change R, C, frequency and drive level; observe the exact first-order transfer function, phase and time-domain behavior.",
            "tone": "Procedure"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "mission2",
          "type": "instruction_card",
          "text": "02 + 03  BUILD ON BREADBOARD",
          "x": 503,
          "y": 208,
          "width": 454,
          "height": 148,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "Follow the illustrated LOW-PASS or HIGH-PASS tab. The circuit uses a single 1 kΩ resistor and 100 nF ceramic capacitor. Keep W1 OFF while moving leads.",
            "tone": "Procedure"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "mission3",
          "type": "instruction_card",
          "text": "04  ACQUIRE FROM AD3",
          "x": 981,
          "y": 208,
          "width": 454,
          "height": 148,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "Verify wiring, select a Physical Device, ARM W1 explicitly, capture simultaneous CH1/CH2 samples and run a frequency sweep. STOP immediately if anything looks wrong.",
            "tone": "Warning"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "mission4",
          "type": "instruction_card",
          "text": "05  ANALYZE + EXPORT",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 374,
          "width": 693,
          "height": 150,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "The Notebook keeps MODEL and AD3 records distinct. Overlay measured gain and phase, evaluate prediction error and export results, reports and captured waveforms.",
            "tone": "Success"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "mission5",
          "type": "instruction_card",
          "text": "REAL EXPERIMENT / REAL QUESTIONS",
          "x": 742,
          "y": 374,
          "width": 693,
          "height": 150,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "What changes at the cutoff frequency? Which component tolerance matters? Does a physical high-pass really approach +90° phase at low frequency? What limits the fit accuracy?",
            "tone": "Information"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "partsTitle",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "BILL OF MATERIALS",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 542,
          "width": 693,
          "height": 40,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Plain Text",
            "wordWrap": false,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "parts",
          "type": "instruction_card",
          "text": "Everything you need",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 590,
          "width": 693,
          "height": 240,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "• Digilent Analog Discovery 3, its flywires, a USB-connected computer and WFScript v0.2-dev.8.8 or newer.\n• One solderless breadboard; 1 kΩ resistor (¼ W); non-polarized 100 nF ceramic capacitor.\n• Short jumper leads; optional DMM to verify continuity and component values.\n• No external power supply, power rail, or external energized circuit is required.",
            "tone": "Procedure"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "safetyTitle",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "IMPORTANT SAFETY / PROVENANCE",
          "x": 742,
          "y": 542,
          "width": 693,
          "height": 40,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "textFormat": "Plain Text",
            "wordWrap": false,
            "borderVisible": true,
            "cornerRadius": 10
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "safetyRules",
          "type": "instruction_card",
          "text": "Before applying any signal",
          "x": 742,
          "y": 590,
          "width": 693,
          "height": 240,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "Never connect W1 to V+, V−, mains, a live external circuit, or a digital input. Keep one shared GND for W1, 1− and 2−. Use CH1+ at VIN and CH2+ at VOUT. Start at ≤1 V peak / 0 V offset, sine only. Verify your breadboard connects exactly as drawn. The Panel cannot detect wiring mistakes or prevent an external fault.",
            "tone": "Warning"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "startFooter",
          "type": "label",
          "text": "PAGES 07–09: Derive the least-squares algorithm, read its JavaScript, and inspect fitted/residual waveforms.",
          "x": 25,
          "y": 848,
          "width": 1410,
          "height": 58,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
