          "x": 422,
          "y": 775,
          "width": 1010,
          "height": 140,
          "value": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "events": {},
          "properties": {
            "body": "Each point commands an AD3 sine wave, waits for analog settling, captures BOTH Scope channels together, fits a sine and cosine at the requested frequency, then computes H = CH2/CH1 and phase(CH2) − phase(CH1). The actual acquisition sampling rate is read back. No fabricated “measured” points are used. On Pages 07–09, derive the fit and inspect real residuals; small residual is not a calibration guarantee.",
